    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442-a1">

                <pb facs="0604" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg498"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 146.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Haberacker to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>288 <hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">St. Clair Street</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Cleveland, Ohio</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1891-08-19"><hi rendition="#italic">August
                                19, 1890</hi>.</date> (Received August 21.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Honorable Sir</hi>: I most respectfully submit the
                    inclosed clipping from a Cleveland paper of this date, which is a correct
                    statement of the facts of arrest, etc., of John Haberacker, my brother, in
                    Bavaria. He reached his twenty-first year yesterday, and had intended to take
                    out his full papers, if necessary, on his return.</p>
                <p>Praying you to see that justice is done him, his parents and the undersigned
                    hopefully await your assistance.</p>
                <p>Yours, most respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George
                    Haberacker</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d442-a1-a1.xml" xpointer="d442-a1-a1"/>
            </div>
